From: Alex Perrin <44126061+AlexPerrin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 09:44:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat: jewellery teleports (games necklace, dueling, glory,
 skills, combat)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Problem. Teleport jewellery did nothing: Rub and the worn destination ops
of the games necklace, ring of dueling, amulet of glory, skills necklace
and combat bracelet had no script.

Change. New module content/travel/jewellery-teleports + pack:
- Rub (held op 4) opens the teleport menu (interface 187 via script 217
  with hotkeys, as RuneLite's Better Teleport Menu expects); the worn ops
  after Remove teleport straight to a destination, in the cache's order.
- Each use takes a charge. Games necklace / ring of dueling: "You rub the
  necklace...", "Your games necklace has seven uses left.", "Your games
  necklace crumbles to dust." on the last one. Glory, skills necklace and
  combat bracelet keep an uncharged item; their lines are "Your amulet has
  three charges left." / "You use your amulet's last charge." for the
  glory and "Your skills necklace has ..." / "You use your skills
  necklace's last charge." (combat bracelet alike) for the others.
- Games necklace / dueling teleport up to level 20 Wilderness, the
  dragonstone items up to level 30 (members).
- Corporeal Beast lands in the lair's safe room at 2964,4382,2 (map square
  46,68). The wiki's games necklace map draws the teleport at 2967,4254
  (square 46,66), but Shortest Path's games necklace tile, its lair cave
  entrance and RuneLite's world map (2967,4384) all put the live lair in
  square 46,68, so the Shortest Path tile is used.
- Farming Guild lands inside the guild (1248,3725) with 45 Farming,
  outside (1248,3719) otherwise.
- dbtables jewellery_teleport_items / _dests (56013-56014, rows
  60294-60350).

Tests. JewelleryTeleportScriptTest (integration, 5): a games necklace use
swaps the item and sends the uses line; the last dueling charge crumbles
and the last glory charge leaves the amulet; no item means no charge;
the glory / skills necklace / combat bracelet charge lines; the Farming
Guild tile at 44 and 45 Farming and the Corporeal Beast tile.

Data sources. OSRS Wiki (by the wiki's contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 3.0):
Games necklace, Ring of dueling, Amulet of glory, Skills necklace (incl.
note a, the 45 Farming rule), Combat bracelet, Farming Guild (boosts may be
used to enter), Wilderness (teleport restrictions). Cache: inventory ops
and worn-op params of the items. Shortest Path hub plugin
(teleportation_items.tsv, transports.tsv): tiles, 4-tick duration, the
Corporeal Beast tile and the Farming Guild inside tile. RuneLite
worldmap/TeleportLocationData.java: Corporeal Beast cross-check. Supplies
Tracker hub plugin (onChatMessage): the "Your amulet has", "your amulet's
last charge", "your skills necklace's last charge", "your combat
bracelet's last charge" prefixes.

Caveats.
- Best guesses: the menu title, the rest of the dragonstone charge lines
  ("... charges left.", "You use ..."; the plugin matches only the
  prefixes, the wiki quotes none), the "You rub the amulet/bracelet..."
  line, the purple value, the 714/111 animation and the missing arrival
  animation.
- The Farming Guild check uses the boosted level, as the guild's door
  does; the wiki does not say so for the teleport.
- The wiki's Corporeal Beast spawn table calls the square 46,68 lair the
  Ironman one; the teleport tile follows the live-data sources above.
- No destination requirements (Tears of Guthix quest, Zeah visit, Hero
  title), landing radius, uncharged Rub message or recharging.

